      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2014 by the Society of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Stress injury is a common cause of exercise-induced anterior shin pain. It is important to distinguish between the various causes of stress injury in a timely manner in order to optimize favorable treatment outcomes. Here, we will discuss a case of medial tibial stress syndrome, or shin splints, as one of the causes of shin pain, as well as how to approach shin pain for a successful diagnosis."
      },
